==Post-match==
U.S. vice president [[Al Gore]], UEFA president [[Lennart Johansson]] and FIFA president [[João Havelange]] were among those present at the stands during the awards ceremony. In the presentation ceremony, Gore handed the trophy to Brazil's captain, Dunga.<ref name="coming"/><ref name="FIFA">{{cite AV media|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pLPM_JSbGvI |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/varchive/youtube/20211221/pLPM_JSbGvI |archive-date=December 21, 2021 |url-status=live|title=Brazil v Italy – The Final – 1994 FIFA World Cup USA|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|date=April 6, 2018|type=YouTube video}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

==In popular culture==
In 2023, Italian comedy metal band [[Nanowar of Steel]] and [[Joakim Brodén]] released a song called "Pasadena 1994" about the match.

